From 375bbd83bacbc32389d58363d9d75ac7ae4259f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 08:48:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0167-v3 -- Lever 3 engine-side routing
 (Pixtone IRQ-mix) + Bug 5 defensive interlock

=== v3 amendment (Bug 5 defensive interlock per flush-instr's #131 sec.24.8) ===

PLAY3 hung at scene transition (bkMoon load) with L3=1 +
AUDIO_BACKEND=opl3 (default). Source-only investigation in flush-
instr's #131 sec.24.5-24.7 could not pin the deep L3+Organya
conflict mechanism. Two adjacent hypotheses remain unresolved:
(a) Organya + SDL3_mixer-Pixtone-fallback resource conflict at
scene transition; (b) engine-spin-waiting-for-Organya-callback
under L3=1. Both are deferred to v1.0.2's deep root-cause
campaign.

For v1.0.1 we make the dangerous combination unrepresentable in
the engine. The v2 cache (env_set && SDL_DOSPixtoneIRQMixActive())
had an init-ordering fragility: SoundManager::init's OPL3 probe
runs AFTER OpenDevice, so when the OPL3 probe falls back to
Organya the cached L3 decision can already be "engaged" while the
live music backend is Organya. The v3 amend closes this race with
a per-call enum compare against NXE::Diag::g_p10_audio_backend_
active:

  * Runs OUTSIDE the lazy cache (every Pixtone::play / setVolume
    call), so a post-init probe fallback is observed immediately.
  * Cheap: one enum compare on a hot already-cached extern; zero
    SDL boundary cross.
  * Emit-once LOG_ERROR ("L3 + ORGANYA IS KNOWN-INCOMPATIBLE;
    forcing L3-OFF") so the operator sees WHY their L3=1
    combination got ignored; explicit reference to v1.0.2 deep
    root-cause campaign + suggested remediations (wb / midi-stub
    or verify OPL3 probe succeeds).
  * Engine NEVER enters any L3 routing branch under this
    combination; Pixtone::play / setVolume short-circuit to the
    existing SDL3_mixer path.

Most-likely-root-cause hypothesis (which this interlock directly
disarms): PLAY3's L3=1 + AUDIO_BACKEND=opl3 default ran through
SoundManager::init's probe chain. On the failing iter, OPL3 probe
returned success at OpenDevice time (so SDL_DOSPixtoneIRQMix
Active() resolved TRUE and the engine-side cache committed to L3
ENGAGED), then a downstream probe step or backend swap reverted
g_p10_audio_backend_active to Organya. At the next Pixtone::play
under the (now stale) "L3 engaged" cache, the engine routed
through SDL_DOSPixtoneStart while the music side ran Organya, hit
one of hypothesis (a) or (b) above, and hung. v1.0.2 verifies.

Architectural invariant captured: ANY engine-side decision that
gates on a music-backend property MUST consult g_p10_audio_
backend_active at the gate-call site, not at first-call cache
population time. The Phase 10 backend-selection chain (probe ->
fallback) is allowed to mutate g_p10_audio_backend_active after
OpenDevice. Caches that snapshot a backend-dependent SDL gate at
first call without re-checking the backend enum will mis-fire if
any later step in the probe chain swaps backends. v2 had this
fragility; v3 closes it for L3. Future levers that depend on the
music backend should follow the same per-call gate pattern (or
explicitly invalidate their cache on backend swap).

TAS-baseline-invariance note: this interlock fires from Pixtone::
play / setVolume call sites which run inside game.tick(); the
LOG_ERROR emit is gated by an emit-once latch so it does not
flood the log nor add per-tick wall-time that could shift TAS
replay state determinism. The interlock branch path itself is
one enum compare + one branch; under the SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_-
PIXTONE_IRQ_MIX-unset default path the branch never enters (the
cached decision is 0 so the interlock predicate fails on the
first conjunct g_pixtone_irq_mix_decided == 1).

=== End v3 amendment; v2 body follows unchanged ===

486-campaign Bug 2 continuous-SFX-stutter -- structural fix engine-
side companion to sdl-engine's SDL/0071. v2 probe iter verdict
confirmed hypothesis C (cooperative-scheduler audio-thread
starvation; max single-callback latency 1701 ms on real DX2-66 per
#120 sec.22). Lever 3 moves Pixtone PCM mix from the cooperative-
thread SDL3_mixer ring path INTO the SB16 IRQ-5 ISR via the new
SDL_DOSPixtone* channel-pool API; the IRQ that owns the DMA buffer
also does the SFX mix, bypassing the cooperative scheduler entirely
for the SFX path.

This patch is the engine-side companion: it routes Pixtone::play /
stop through SDL_DOSPixtoneStart / Stop when the L3 killswitch is
ENABLED, mirrors setVolume gain into per-slot gain_x256 for
SDL_DOSPixtoneStart consumption, DPMI-locks raw_master_buf so the
ISR mix loop can safely read across IRQ context, and extends the
0165 probe to SUM both counters (g_pixtone_active_count +
g_dos_pixtone_active_count) so the discriminator pillar 2
(max_active_count) contract preserves across both paths.

Author work locked at 13 STOP-and-ack questions across two design
passes (Lever 1 + Lever 3 ack thread; flush-instr sign-off; sec.10
contract locked at L3-Q5 Shape B SUM-both-counters + the three-
iteration discipline that caught the Shape A bug).

Mechanism:

Killswitch -- SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PIXTONE_IRQ_MIX. v1 default OFF
(opt-in via "=1"). HW-IO risk class per [[dosbox_not_proxy]]: a
DPMI page-fault inside the ISR hard-freezes real HW; lever ships
dormant until operator opts in + iter validates. Sentinel-cached
on first pixtone_irq_mix_active() call -- single SDL_GetHint then
cached int; banner emit "pixtone IRQ-mix: ENABLED (opt-in)" /
"pixtone IRQ-mix: DISABLED (default)" on the decision. Same idiom
as nxengine/0162-v2 (MIDGAP_PUMP) / 0164 (TICKPUMP) / 0165 (probe).

Routing branch in Pixtone::play -- when killswitch ENABLED AND
raw_master_buf is populated (the master rendered chunk; not
playResampled's lazy-allocated resampled buffers), route to
SDL_DOSPixtoneStart with the per-slot raw_master_buf + len +
gain_x256 + loop flag. On success, store the returned ISR-pool
channel id in _sound_fx[slot].channel and set on_irq_pool = true
so Pixtone::stop routes correctly later. On pool exhaustion
(SDL_DOSPixtoneStart returns -1), drop the SFX with LOG_DEBUG --
legitimate resource-pressure outcome, not an error. Pool size N=8
matches DOOM canonical + Lever 1 cap.

Routing branch in Pixtone::stop -- if on_irq_pool is true, route
to SDL_DOSPixtoneStop and clear channel + flag. SDL_DOSPixtoneStop
is a no-op if the channel has already ended naturally (the ISR
decrement already fired); calling it unconditionally is safe. If
on_irq_pool is false (the slot was started via SDL3_mixer path),
fall through to the existing MIX_StopTrack body unchanged.

Routing disambiguator -- new bool on_irq_pool field in stPXSound,
default-false. Pixtone::play sets it true under L3 ON; Pixtone::
playResampled (always SDL3_mixer in v1) sets it false; Pixtone::
play SDL3_mixer-fallback path sets it false; Pixtone::stop reads
it to decide the routing branch. 1 byte per stPXSound x 256 slots
= negligible memory cost.

setVolume gain mirror + L3 caveat -- per-slot gain_x256 (int16
fixed-point; 256 = 1.0) added to stPXSound. setVolume converts
volume_0_100 to gain_x256 and mirrors across all _sound_fx[] +
the global g_global_gain_x256. Under L3 ON, SDL_DOSPixtoneStart
reads the per-slot gain_x256 at play time; mid-play volume
updates are no-op (the ISR mixer uses gain captured at start
time). One-shot LOG_INFO caveat banner emitted on first L3-active
setVolume so operator sees the named cause if a scripted fadeout
sounds wrong. v2 candidate: SDL_DOSPixtoneSetGain API for live
per-channel updates.

raw_master_buf DPMI lock -- _go32_dpmi_lock_data call at the end
of Pixtone::_prepareToPlay (right after raw_master_buf + len
assignment) so the SB16 IRQ-5 ISR mix loop can safely read across
IRQ context. Unconditional boot-time lock (all rendered slots) per
L3-Q1 STOP-and-ack: one-time cost ~few ms at boot for ~86 slots;
no race window (lock in place before any ISR could fire); L3-OFF
path leaves the lock dormant (negligible CWSDPMI lock-table
bookkeeping). Wrapped in #ifdef __DJGPP__ for cross-platform build
safety (the lock is a DOS-only concern).

Probe (0165) compat -- extern decl for SDL-side
g_dos_pixtone_active_count (counter atomically maintained by
SDL/0071's SDL_DOSPixtoneStart engine-thread ++ + SB16 IRQ-5 ISR
end-of-buffer --; dual-writer atomicity via __sync_fetch_and_add /
_sub on i486+ = lock xadd / xsub per the L3-Q5 contract). The
[pixtone-multi] audit's live= field + SamplePixtoneActiveBucket's
histogram bucket calculation BOTH SUM the engine + SDL counters at
read time. Under L3 OFF, g_dos_pixtone_active_count is 0 and SUM
equals g_pixtone_active_count -- byte-identical-at-log-level to
pre-0167. Under L3 ON, the SUM captures L3 ISR-pool channels that
don't increment the SDL3_mixer counter. Discriminator pillar 2
(max_active_count) contract preserved across both paths.

v1 scope:

- Pixtone::play non-resampled ONLY -- the polar-star path; the
  Bug-2 target per #120 sec.22 + sec.21.4 verdict.
- Pixtone::playResampled stays SDL3_mixer in v1 -- the resampled
  buffers are lazy-allocated per (slot, percent) pair, requiring
  extra eager-render + DPMI-lock work that's deferred to v2.
  Stream SFX (SND_STREAM1/2/PROPELLOR) play via the SDL3_mixer
  path even under L3 ON. No operator complaint about stream-SFX
  stutter so this is acceptable v1 scope.
- Mid-play setVolume is no-op under L3 ON. Caveat banner emits
  once; v2 candidate.

Default-OFF byte-identity:

- pixtone_irq_mix_active() short-circuits to false (cached int
  compare per call; ~1 cycle). No SDL_DOSPixtone* calls execute.
- on_irq_pool stays false on all slots (only the L3 ON branch
  sets it true). Pixtone::stop reads false and falls through to
  the existing SDL3_mixer body.
- gain_x256 is populated on every setVolume (under both paths),
  but unused if L3 never engages. ~80 stores per setVolume call;
  setVolume is rare (~once per option-screen interaction);
  negligible.
- _go32_dpmi_lock_data is called unconditionally for every
  rendered SFX -- runs at boot, not in the hot path; lock-table
  entries are dormant if L3 never engages.
- Probe SUM uses g_dos_pixtone_active_count = 0 under L3 OFF;
  byte-identical-at-log-level.

The only behavioral change with L3 OFF is the banner LOG_INFO
emitted on first pixtone_irq_mix_active() call ("DISABLED
(default)") -- one line per process; matches the 0162-v2 / 0163
/ 0164 / 0165 banner-only-no-state-change pattern.

Cross-patch dep:

- patches/SDL/0071 provides SDL_DOSPixtoneStart / Stop / IsActive
  declarations in <SDL3/SDL_dospixtone.h> + the atomic
  g_dos_pixtone_active_count counter. Build won't link until
  both patches are on disk. git apply --check is independent.
- Patch builds atop vendor/nxengine-evo head 2b28775 (0165
  post-amend; the 0166 slot is reserved for the potential v3
  cleanup of the broken Organya hook from sec.21.5 -- separate
  patch, deferred per team-lead's "fold OR separate" choice).

Files in this patch:

- src/sound/Pixtone.h        -- 2 extern decls + 2 new stPXSound
